# Expo environment variables for @forge/mobile
# ------------------------------------------------
# Local dev: pull secrets from Doppler
#   pnpm fetch-secrets
#   (writes to .env.local — highest priority, gitignored)
#
# EAS builds: env vars come from EAS Environments (expo.dev dashboard)
#   Preview    -> "preview" environment
#   Production -> "production" environment

# ── Admin GraphQL endpoint (optional) ────────────────────────────────
# Leave it unset. A development bundle already defaults to local admin
# (http://localhost:3003/api/graphql, rewritten to 10.0.2.2 on the
# Android emulator); a release bundle defaults to production admin.
#
# To point somewhere else — a LAN IP for a physical device, a tunnel —
# put it in .env.development.local, NOT here and NOT in .env.local:
#   - fetch-secrets replaces .env.local wholesale, so a value there is
#     silently lost on the next run
#   - .env.development.local is never loaded in production mode, so it
#     cannot be inlined into an `expo export` / `eas update` bundle
#
#   echo 'EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMIN_GRAPHQL_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3003/api/graphql' \
#     > apps/mobile/.env.development.local
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMIN_GRAPHQL_URL=

# ── Allow a development build to use production admin (optional) ─────
# A development bundle that resolves to admin.jesusfilm.org refuses to
# start: a local session writes search events and search traces into the
# production database. Set this in .env.development.local to opt in
# deliberately; the startup line then names production every launch.
# Any non-empty value works. Cold-restart Metro after changing it.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_ADMIN=1

# ── Admin consumer bearer (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# Sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` ONLY on the Search operation
# (admin's SEARCH_AUTH_REQUIRED gate). Public queries (watchSetting,
# experienceBySlug, videoBySlug) stay anonymous on purpose: a bearer'd
# request rate-limit-buckets as consumer:<key> on admin — ONE shared
# bucket for every install carrying the key — while anonymous requests
# bucket per device IP.
#
# Provisioning rules:
# - The value must be a DEDICATED entry in admin's WEB_ADMIN_API_KEYS
#   CSV minted for mobile — never reuse apps/web SSR's or apps/tv's
#   value, or revoking one surface breaks the others.
# - Sequencing: add the entry to admin's CSV and deploy admin FIRST,
#   then set this var in EAS Environments / Doppler, then build.
# - Rotation: a key baked into shipped binaries can't change without a
#   store release — keep old + new CSV entries overlapping until old
#   app versions age out.
# Local dev: set in .env.local and cold-restart Metro (values inline at
# bundle time).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMIN_GRAPHQL_TOKEN=
